    "long_instructions": "You are building a classifier to identify whether text messages are spam or not. The code for training the classifier has been written for you, but you need to complete the `get_features` function, which accepts a text message as input and returns a dictionary of all the features the classifier will use to determine if a message is spam or not.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Count how many exclamation points appear in the message. Save this in a variable called `exclamation_count`.\r\n2. Count how many dollar signs appear in the message. Save this in a variable called `dollar_sign_count`.\r\n3. Count how many words are written in all caps (in other words, the word has multiple letters that are all uppercase). Save this in a variable called `all_caps_words`.\r\n4. Once you’re done, run your program a few times and pay attention to what kinds of accuracy scores you get.\r\n\r\nYou can use AI Tutor to help you with working with strings if you get stuck!\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nSince `message` is a string, you can treat it as a sequence of characters that you can loop over. For example, a loop might begin with a line like:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfor character in message:\r\n```\r\n",
